Z||000000||Racer 1||11-25-1999||10:20 PM||||Damn I didnt know so many people were selling Fiero parts on E-Bay! GT front fascia's for $50.00.Whole fieros for cheap sometimes. I got a bid on the Fiero manuals out of a 1986 coupe. I dont have these black books. <BR> <A HREF="http://fierorob.homepage.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://fierorob.homepage.com/</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||ggarsk||11-26-1999||01:50 AM||||They are selling them because it is a good way to make money. If you watch some of the items they go for a good price(for the seller). I've bought a bunch of items of of e-bay. I've paid what I wanted to pay. Other things I didn't get cuase I couldn't justify spending so much money for it. It just depends on how bad you need or want that item.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||11-26-1999||09:54 AM||||I sometimes use eBay to buy record albums (I have a minor collection). You have to be careful about bidding and not get caught up in bidding wars. I've "stole" cheap items before by waiting until the last second to bid, this keeps others from "upping" their bids too. I always keep the shipping cost in mind also. I've bought several albums for less than the shipping charges, which basically doubles the price. If the bidding goes above your max price, then forget it, another item will be along again eventually. Be careful, eBay is addictive, but they do have a 12 step help program for eBay.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||11-26-1999||09:57 AM||||Some prices are just rediculous on there.  Ash trays going for $13 right now.  Drive down to GM and get a pair brand new for $5.  There are others but the ash trays always seem to stick out when I see them, going for that price.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||11-26-1999||11:45 AM||||One thing to remember, some people live in remote areas. I live in the middle of nowhere too, but I traveling a lot (for both business and pleasure), but not everyone can. Maybe to them $20 ashtrays (figuring in shipping) is a great deal compared to driving over the mountain range on rutted gravel roads to the nearest city. Then again, some people have more money than they have time (or brains sometimes).||||reg||1
