Z||000008||batboy||11-27-1999||12:19 AM||||That Fiero still has 6 days left to go. What usually happens is that the item will stay fairly low until the last day or so or even the last few hours, then bidding goes crazy. Keep on eye on it though, if it's still very low towards the end, you may want to make an offer. Personally, buying a car "sight unseen" does not appeal to me. Maybe getting burnt on a $5 record album through eBay is one thing, but getting burnt for hundreds or even thousands of dollars on a bad car is another story.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Racer 1||11-27-1999||03:04 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">Yeah I would probably want to test drive the car first. It could be a complete LEMON with nice skin? Thats alot of money to be laying down for a pic on the computer!! One thing thats kinda fishy is in the discription of the car the guy said he went to the "car lot" about the power steering goof. Now what happened if they sold it at the car lot before E-Bay bid would close?<p>[This message has been edited by Racer 1 (edited 11-27-1999).]||||reg||6
Z||000010||DJRice||11-29-1999||09:11 AM||||I have acquired quite a collection of Hot Wheels Fieros via Ebay.  Of course, the average price per each car has been about $2-$3.  Thats expensive for Hot Wheels, but hey, they are Fieros, and I think I have them all.  I even have a GT Model that is painted Camoflauge and has hugh tires, missle launchers, and a machine gun on it.  (HW Action Fleet).<P>Where else could I get a fully armed Fiero attack vehicle for $2.50?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||RossT||12-02-1999||12:44 AM||||Ebay can be very addicting, but you know, so is this forum!! I check in numerous times every day (at home and at work). Using Batboys advice, I finally go my pontiac 22-p parts book from e-bay. I waited till there was 30 seconds on the auction then placed my bid. I have been trying to get this book since last April, but I was always outbid.  The book up until recently was sold by a company called THULE?. They ran out not to long ago. FOCA sells them for $30 but they would nevery return an e-mail message inquiring about stock. I tried severy times no response.  Thus I had to resort to e-bay. I paid way to much for a new one $44.00, but I really wanted that book. Last April I saw one sell for $76. And you thought the sunroof<BR>case and shade sold for big bucks.<P>Thanks Batboy,<BR>Ross.||||reg||1
